eted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\r\n### [REQUIRED] Searched documentation and issues\r\nSearched the exoplayer issues for the error \"cannot find symbol class Nullable\" and did not find it.\r\nSearched the exoplayer dev site https://exoplayer.dev/ for \"cannot find symbol class Nullable\" and did not find it.\r\n\r\n### [REQUIRED] Question\r\nI am building an exoplayer app and cloning the repository and depending on the modules locally as described here: https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer#locally .   When I build the app, I get these errors when ExoPlayer\\extensions\\ima\\src\\main\\java\\com\\google\\android\\exoplayer2\\ext\\ima\\ImaAdsLoader.java is compiled:\r\n\r\nerror: cannot find symbol class IntDef\r\nerror: cannot find symbol class VisibleForTesting\r\nerror: cannot find symbol class Nullable\r\n\r\nInterestingly, if I clone Exoplayer from github and build it, I do not see these errors.  It is only when I build my app that depends on the local exoplayer libraries that I get the errors.   I noticed that several other exoplayer extensions, such as exoplayer-extension-okhttp, also use the Nullable symbol from androidx.annotation:annotation:1.0.2.  However, the other extensions include the dependency\r\n\r\nimplementation 'androidx.annotation:annotation:1.0.2'\r\n\r\nin their build.gradle file.\r\n\r\nIf I add implementation 'androidx.annotation:annotation:1.0.2' to the exoplayer-extension-ima build.gradle file, my app builds with no errors.\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- DO NOT DELETE\r\nvalidate_template=true\r\ntemplate_path=.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/question.md\r\n-->\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"andrewlewis","id":107897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzg5Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewlewis","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewlewis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/use